    "erv-join-lead": {
      "id": "erv-join-lead",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The reader joins what each adapter returns on all 6 tags: engine, run_id, node_path, invocation_id, attempt_id and loop_path. A row with no Archon facts still gets a place, so a run that only the tags show still gives a tree."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "erv-join": {
      "id": "erv-join",
      "type": "structured-table",
      "props": {
        "columns": [
          "Rule",
          "As the code applies it"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "A row belongs to a node attempt",
            [
              {
                "insert": "All 6 tags are equal. "
              },
              {
                "insert": "normalizeTags",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": " first maps an empty tag to null, and null equals only null."
              }
            ]
          ],
          [
            "A kernel container belongs to a node attempt",
            "The kernel adapter lists the containers with the run's engine and run_id tags and keeps each one with an attempt_id. A container inside the container of another attempt stays part of that attempt's trace."
          ],
          [
            "A call counts as a gateway call",
            [
              {
                "insert": "isServedCall",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": ": the outcome is not "
              },
              {
                "insert": "relayed",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": ", and the response id does not start with "
              },
              {
                "insert": "resp_prewarm_",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": ". An empty outcome counts."
              }
            ]
          ],
          [
            "The call count of a node attempt",
            "The served calls with the attempt's 6 tags that have reached ClickHouse. A kernel node counts its calls and lists its kernel spans in their place."
          ],
          [
            "A skipped node",
            [
              {
                "insert": "A "
              },
              {
                "insert": "node_skipped",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": " row of "
              },
              {
                "insert": "archon.db",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": " gives an attempt with status skipped. A "
              },
              {
                "insert": "node_skipped_prior_success",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": " row of a resumed run gives one with no attempt id."
